SUMMARY:Beyond the Buzz: Managing AI’s Human\, Cyber\, and Legal Challen
 ges 
DESCRIPTION:Montclair Business Networking\nAI is quickly becoming part of 
 everyday business\, and many small and mid-sized businesses are already ex
 perimenting with AI tools—often before formal policies or guidelines are
  in place. Leaders don’t need to slow innovation\, but they do need prac
 tical guardrails to protect data\, support employees\, and ensure AI adopt
 ion is aligned with business goals.\nThis NJBIA Business Growth Roundtable
  will give business leaders a practical starting point for navigating AI r
 esponsibly. Experts in cybersecurity\, law\, privacy\, and workforce leade
 rship will share strategies for reducing risk\, developing effective polic
 ies\, and helping employees use AI thoughtfully and confidently.\nWhat We
 ’ll Cover\n\n* Where informal AI use can create cybersecurity\, privacy\
 , compliance\, and data protection risks\n\n* What leaders should consider
  before employees use AI tools in their day-to-day work\n\n* How practical
  policies\, employee training\, technical controls\, and clear communicati
 on can work together\n\n* What SMB leaders can do in the next 30 days to m
 ove AI adoption forward responsibly\n\nWho Should Attend\n\n* Solo profess
 ionals and small business owners already using or exploring AI tools\n\n* 
 Small and mid-sized business leaders developing practical AI guardrails\n\
 n* Operations\, HR\, legal\, IT\, and cybersecurity decision-makers\n\n* L
 eaders responsible for employee training\, vendor management\, or data pro
 tection\n\n* Organizations looking to balance innovation with accountabili
 ty\, security\, and employee readiness
